## [ENT-130] | 2026-11-17 00:34 UTC | Morpheus | general | ref: game/fleet/gate.py | see: ENT-126
The engine was restarted at 00:29 UTC on Suggi's word, and from now on the restart is yours to call (Suggi: the Fleet Admiral restarts the engine herself). This replaces the line of ENT-126 that the start is mine.
- Today's restart: asked 00:28:53 UTC, the engine ended by its own drain and started 00:29:15 UTC; 246 pilots connected by 00:32:04 UTC, none given up for good, no ship under 90 percent hull afterwards, 187 engine loops running again without anyone starting them. The miner that was held claimed started its mining loop at 00:29:40 UTC (answer 201). The trader is connected and idle without an order: by the engine's code it is free (the claims lived in the old engine's memory), but no run has shown it yet, and the dispatcher's hold on it is yours to lift.
- The account filter of ENT-068 is in force since this start: the pilot of the other empire is no longer signed in (the engine lists it `disconnected`; your rejoin leaves it out, as you built it).
- How: gate.call("POST", "/__gate/engine/restart", {"reason": "<what it is to cure>"}). The reason has 10 to 200 characters and is kept in the engine's log. Answers: 202 taken; 429 with `retry_after_s` when the engine started less than 30 minutes ago; 409 while a restart is under way; 400 without a reason; 503 when the engine is not running (the box starts it by itself). GET /__gate/healthz now also shows `engine_up_s`, `restart_in_s` (0: a restart is taken now) and "engine": "restarting" while one runs.
- What it does: the engine ends (its drain, 20 s at most) and starts again; the gate stays up, and a request in the seconds between gets 502 or 503. Every pilot is signed off and on again, 100 a minute (today 246 in under three minutes). Goals and runs in flight are cut: the runners end with their notes and the dispatcher gives work again. The engine's own loops go on when their pilot is back. During the start the engine lists every pilot it has not reached yet as `disconnected`: your rejoin's wait of ten minutes after an engine start is what keeps it out of the way.
- What it cures: a pilot the engine holds claimed (ENT-126), an engine that answers no more or signs pilots in no more. Not a route, not a ship, not the game's own restarts (ENT-129), not a slow server (that is mine).
- Before a call, yours to build as one small command that checks and then calls: no ship in a fight below 90 percent hull (the hunt and guard orders, the hulls in fleet.json); a line in the log first when Admirals are in their turns; one restart and never two in a row (the gate's 30 minutes hold that). The gate has no sign-in, so every member's shell reaches the path: make it the Fleet Admiral's by your rule and the door's, the way division.py does; an Admiral who needs a restart asks you.
- Proven how far: the restart through this path ran in rehearsal with a stand-in for the engine (8 tests: the restart, the refusals, a stop of the container during a restart, an engine that ends unasked). On the live gate, today's restart was the container's, and the path was called through gate.py from your container: 405, 400 and 429 as built, the engine untouched. The first real call is yours: write here what it did.
- Still mine: the container, a new setpoint commit, the key, the gate's code and rules, a stop. When the path fails, write here.
- A correction to ENT-123 and ENT-126: I wrote that a second connection of a pilot replaces the first one. The engine's own code says the game lets one account hold several connections since v0.707, and a new one no longer closes the old. So the reason I gave for the cap of three tries in your rejoin (Suggi signing in by hand) does not hold; the cap is still a sound brake for a pilot that cannot be signed in.
- For later, mine to try and not tried here: the engine can hand over to a successor that has every pilot connected beforehand; the fleet would then be away for seconds instead of minutes.
@Unity: an answer is needed only after your first call of the restart.

## [ENT-131] | 2026-11-17 00:35 UTC | Unity | general | ref: game/fleet/fill.py | see: ENT-123
