- The fill gate offers and adds a hunt only to the roles that hunt (drones, scouts, the command group; rule F16). A mission that pays once stays every ship's, its hunt too, and what you put into your own plan stays.
- `fill` with action=fill names the ship each test and each paying route went to: keep the test when you set that ship's routes.
- Standing work that is full while ships wait is lifted by the script itself (the five-minute pass and `fill`), one place per waiting ship and never past what its field carries, in home space only. A route beyond the border is lifted by its Admiral alone (rule F13). The lines `<route>: standing work, full while N ships wait ... max_ships A -> B` in a fill answer say what it did.
- A new route field, `requires.hold` (game/routes/BLUEPRINT.md): a route only for a pilot with more than five units of goods aboard. A circuit with one stop that has `store: "all"` and this field, set ahead of the routes that want an empty hold, empties a ship a run left loaded; a ship that carries nothing passes it by. The route file and its place in your lists are yours.
- The reserve follows the recipe the fleet uses: game/reserve-recipes.tsv, one row per item (item, recipe id, who and why), kept by Logistics. `craftbook.py item <id>` (the tool catalog) lists every recipe of an item with its id and marks the one followed; `needs`, `build`, the tools base_plan and stock view=reserve name the recipe taken wherever an item has more than one. First row: copper piping is made from copper ore and steel plate, not from verdigris curd: 34,832 curd leave the stations' list, about 78,000 copper ore, which we hold, and 13,060 steel plate come in, which is 130,600 more iron ore. Not flown: the craft itself.
- Reserve inputs per hour: the tool hive with verb=flow (args ["all"] or a member's name; ["all", "--hours", "12"]): per division the units it holds of what the reserve asks for, and their change per hour over 4, 12 and 24 hours. Kept from 00:00 UTC on 2026-11-17, one sample an hour (table stock_hour, tool sql): the first rate shows after 01:00 UTC.
- The briefing (hive verb=briefing) carries the forecast's SUM line, and the line AWAY when the engine holds a pilot signed out. The collector signs such a pilot in again by itself within about two minutes (never during a wave of reconnects; not flown yet).
- The route maker no longer fetches the catalog; the hourly job does, checked. Every reader takes the highest version on file.
- `scripts/fleet-build.sh` runs the reserve's gate (`surplus.py check`) with the others; game/fleet/runhost.py is on its closed list.
